# Reflection - Unit 2: Building App UI

## What I Learned
- How to use conditionals, classes, function types, and lambda expressions in Kotlin.
- The concept of handling user actions (like button clicks).
- How state can be used to calculate and update values, such as in a tip calculator.

## Challenges
- Understanding lambda expressions and function types required practice.
- Simulating UI interactions in pure Kotlin was limited compared to Android Studio.
- Translating logic into user interface behavior was a new skill.

## My Choices
- I wrote Kotlin-only simulations for button clicks and state handling to practice logic outside Android Studio.
- I used simple examples (score evaluation, tip calculator) to reinforce fundamentals.
- I focused on clean, readable code with comments.

## Outcome
Unit 2 strengthened my Kotlin fundamentals and introduced me to interactive app concepts.  
Even without Android Studio UI, I practiced the logic behind buttons and state, preparing me for full app development in later units.

